# UI theme — tokens, not remaps

Light and dark are defined **once** in `apps/web/src/app/globals.css` (`:root` vs `.dark`). Screens must consume those tokens. Do not add `text-white` + CSS remaps, `bg-[#0f0f0f]`, or `[color-scheme:dark]`.

## Tokens

Use these (they already switch with the theme):

| Token | Light | Dark |
|---|---|---|
| `--background` / `--page-bg` | zinc-50 / zinc-100 | zinc-950 / zinc-900 |
| `--foreground` | zinc-900 | zinc-50 |
| `--muted` | zinc-600 | zinc-400 |
| `--card` / `--card-bg` | white (solid) | zinc-900 / white 4% |
| `--border` | zinc-200 | zinc-800 |
| `--input` / `--input-bg` | white (solid) | zinc-900 / white 6% |
| `--primary` / `--primary-foreground` | black / white | white / black |
| `--hover` | black 5% | white 6% |
| `--overlay` | black 40% | black 60% |

Tailwind aliases: `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `bg-card`, `bg-background`, `border-border`, `bg-input`.

## Standard elements

| UI | Classes |
|---|---|
| Selected / active fill | `fill-primary` or `bg-primary text-primary-foreground` |
| Primary action | `btn btn-primary btn-sm` (or `btn-md` / `btn-lg`) |
| Secondary / cancel | `btn btn-secondary btn-sm` |
| Ghost | `btn btn-ghost btn-sm` |
| Icon-only | `icon-btn` |
| Text/select/textarea | `input` |
| Field caption | `label` |
| Card / section | `card` |
| Modal / drawer panel | `sheet` |
| Dropdown | `popover` |
| Backdrop | `overlay` |
| Chip / pill | `chip` |
| List row | `list-row` |
| Menu row | `menu-item` |
| Progress | `progress` + `progress-bar` |
| Secondary copy | `muted` |

## Do not

```tsx
// BAD — dark-first utilities (light mode then fights them with remaps)
<div className="bg-[#0f0f0f] text-white border-white/10">
<input className="bg-white/6 text-white [color-scheme:dark]" />
```

```tsx
// GOOD — tokens switch for you
<div className="sheet">
  <h3 className="text-foreground">Add budget item</h3>
  <label className="label">Category</label>
  <select className="input">…</select>
  <button className="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Save</button>
</div>
```

Hardcoded red/amber for overdue/warning is fine. Brand `gold-*` is zinc now — do not use it for “accent gold.”

Selected/active must pair fill with ink. `--primary` is black in light and white in dark. Never `color: '#fff'` on `var(--color-brand-primary)` — that is white-on-white in dark mode. Use `var(--color-primary-foreground)`.
